WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.073
- Okay.

00:00:01.073 --> 00:00:03.580
This is the story of the first time

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.820
that I told somebody I loved them.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.903
(gentle piano music)

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:15.070
- Um, I feel many will say that it was

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.950
a beautiful day like today
in front of a fountain

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.560
with the music playing the back,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.310
but it was, we were just in her home,

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.790
we were just watching TV on her bed,

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:30.160
and while watching the
show, I couldn't focus

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.290
on what was going on in the movie

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.180
because I was taken by the emotions

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.290
I was starting to realize
and feel out of nowhere,

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.680
and I just looked at her and I told her

00:00:41.248 --> 00:00:42.081
that I love you.

00:00:42.081 --> 00:00:45.800
And it was because I really did feel it.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.620
I felt like I needed her to know

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.300
because you never know if
tomorrow was granted or not.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.490
Her reciprocating it was
like the pillow I needed

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.550
because saying I love you is so risky,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.620
and if I'm dropping my
head back and you don't

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.700
hear it back or say it back,

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.190
you're just gonna slam
your head really hard

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.500
into something, but she was that pillow

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.950
that kind of reassured me, like everything

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.260
is gonna be all right.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.210
- We had been dating for a
month, which really isn't

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.500
that long, but I just felt it, I knew it,

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.730
I knew it was different.

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.610
And I really wanted him to say it first

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.150
because I was too scared.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.080
So I remember one night
when I was saying goodbye

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.180
because we were doing kind
of a long distance thing,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.963
I was hugging him, and
I was saying I really,

00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:28.780
I really, really like you.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.150
And he was like yeah, I
really, really like you too.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.810
But I was really digging into it.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.760
I was like, no you don't get.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.847
I really like you.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.410
And I was listing off all these things

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.870
that I love about him,
like I love his smile,

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.730
I love his hair, I love his
laugh, I love his kindness,

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.380
I love his personality.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.580
And he caught on.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.173
And he just said I love you.

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:53.270
And I was just like yes.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.430
I love you too.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.220
I kind of pushed him into it a little bit,

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.563
but he wanted to say it
too, so it worked out.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.700
- It's kind of embarrassing.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.040
And I probably should like
never go online and admit this,

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.763
but I told someone I loved
them and then I farted.

00:02:11.781 --> 00:02:12.614
And they heard it.

00:02:12.614 --> 00:02:14.710
I was like, I hope they didn't hear that.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.010
And they did.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.140
They definitely heard it.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.680
I was like getting out of
the car, and I was like

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.840
love you, and it's like
one of those things

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.230
that like slips when you
didn't want to say it yet,

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.760
and then you did.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.519
And as I was getting
out of the car I farted.

00:02:26.519 --> 00:02:28.815
(laughing)

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.190
And I was just like hope
they didn't hear that.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.340
And they were like, I did.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.350
I've changed since then.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.940
Now I've learned to fart
earlier on with people

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.140
so that way if it accidentally slips out

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.886
I can just be like, I
totally planned that.

00:02:40.886 --> 00:02:43.470
(laughing)

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.680
Oh that is so wholesome.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.330
Okay, bye.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.430
(laughing) All right.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.630
- I think the first time I
told someone I loved them

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.970
would have been my best
friend at the time.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.803
It was mutual.

00:02:57.803 --> 00:02:59.400
(laughs) We loved each other.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.290
And I think I even gave her
a little blue ring I had.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.683
That was before I was interested in boys.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.530
That first love is so innocent.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.340
You're not looking for anything.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.570
You are a blank slate, and
you just know what you love,

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.450
and it's straight from the heart.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.610
Later on, you look for things.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:23.160
You look for qualities, or
there's a blueprint later on,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.900
but in the first love is
just straight from the heart.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.860
Doesn't matter what someone looks like.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.730
Doesn't matter if
they're your best friend.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.410
It doesn't matter what sex they are,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.630
it doesn't matter how
much money they have.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.790
It's just from the heart.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.853
- The first time I told
somebody I loved them

00:03:37.853 --> 00:03:39.590
I was probably in kindergarten.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.870
His Lego, or I think it was like a GI Joe

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.345
got stuck in a tree and I got it

00:03:43.345 --> 00:03:44.950
because I was the only tall one.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.970
And he gave me a kiss on the cheek

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.320
and I told him I loved him.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.380
- I never really knew what love was.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.260
I thought I did.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.610
It was something I always wanted,

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.600
but I never knew what it was, honestly.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.913
Until I met this one right here.

00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:05.270
(giggling)

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.472
You know, I've had, I guess
they call it puppy love.

00:04:07.472 --> 00:04:09.910
I don't know, I thought it was love.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:14.200
But when I met him, that's
when I experienced love.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.230
You lose yourself in puppy love

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.810
because you're so about the other person.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.580
I don't know, you lose who you are.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.160
You feel like you're
tolerating their behavior.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.750
He asked me, how do I tolerate him?

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.387
And normally when somebody
asks me that question

00:04:27.387 --> 00:04:29.480
I'm like because, this, this, this.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.453
But when he asked me that, I was like,

00:04:31.453 --> 00:04:33.203
I don't tolerate you, I love you.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.320
- [Thoraya] Can you explain the setting,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.613
how you said it exactly?

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.162
- We were in the bed.

00:04:40.162 --> 00:04:41.716
(laughs)

00:04:41.716 --> 00:04:45.010
We were in the bed, and
I was just describing

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.820
everything I love about him,

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.620
but I didn't say I love you.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.210
And then he asked me, he
said you love everything else

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.292
about me but me.

00:04:54.292 --> 00:04:56.246
And I was like, I do love you.

00:04:56.246 --> 00:04:58.340
So that was my first
time saying I love him.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.520
It's different. It's different.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.620
You'll know it when you got it, I promise.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.583
You will know it.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.550
Like, that's my husband.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.730
Next time y'all see us,
you'll see us married.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:09.603
I'm telling you.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:23.350
- So, when I was 16 I had a boyfriend,

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.720
and he would always say I love YouTube.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.910
I love YouTube.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.760
Just so he wouldn't have to say I love you

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.166
like when we were first starting dating

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:32.999
because we were just awkward.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.130
And he's like a really funny ginger.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.080
And so one day, he's like I love you.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.380
And I was like, tube?

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.713
And he was like, no tube.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.640
And that was how we said I
love you for the first time

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.543
because we were dumb and 16 years old.

00:05:46.543 --> 00:05:49.240
- I don't think I ever really have.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.410
I just remember,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:53.120
I had an ex-girlfriend,
I cared for her a lot

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.430
but I don't think I
ever actually told her,

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.860
just not a direct I love you.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.090
- [Thoraya] So how
would you express to her

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.040
that you loved her?

00:06:00.992 --> 00:06:01.825
- I don't know, we just spent

00:06:01.825 --> 00:06:03.010
a lot of time together, obviously.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.698
How we shared a lot of the hardships,

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.590
a lot of darkness we both carried.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.600
- [Thoraya] So you were feeling it,

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.870
but you didn't?

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:10.730
- Looking back, yeah.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.917
It definitely was, but I don't know.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:14.683
I guess,

00:06:16.383 --> 00:06:17.300
(laughs) it's weird, I don't know.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.613
I never really thought
about it till now, actually.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.670
Hmm.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.963
Kind of missed opportunity I guess.

00:06:23.963 --> 00:06:25.963
- [Thoraya] Have you been in love since?

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.090
- Not like that.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:32.350
- It was actually over
text, because I'm dumb,

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.917
and I couldn't properly
express myself then,

00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:39.480
and so I was feeling kind of sad,

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.953
and he's just really nice.

00:06:41.953 --> 00:06:43.870
I'm gonna start crying.

00:06:47.121 --> 00:06:47.954
And

00:06:50.223 --> 00:06:52.793
he's like, my shoulder to lean on.

00:06:53.975 --> 00:06:55.275
And I just love him a lot.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.797
So I told him I loved him.

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:01.230
He said I think I love you, too.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.122
I love him

00:07:05.212 --> 00:07:08.379
more than all the stars in the galaxy.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.353
- I never told anyone that I love you.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.400
That I love him, or her.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.200
- [Thoraya] And what'd
you tell me earlier?

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.500
- And I hope that,

00:07:28.386 --> 00:07:29.604
not recording, please.

00:07:29.604 --> 00:07:30.915
(laughing)

00:07:30.915 --> 00:07:33.110
(speaking foreign language)

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:35.870
And I hope that I never do it.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.820
- [Thoraya] You hope that you never--

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.813
- Never say anyone, I love you.

00:07:39.849 --> 00:07:41.330
- [Thoraya] Why is that?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.540
- Because I don't see the point.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.410
Everyone say I love you.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.810
I want to say anything else.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.471
Anything different.

00:07:49.471 --> 00:07:52.800
Something that really means something,

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.540
I don't know how to say
yeah, I think this meaning

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.450
of I love you is empty.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.907
We say I love that thing, oh I love

00:08:01.907 --> 00:08:04.690
(speaking foreign
language) that something.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:09.683
But when you either find
the person who actually,

00:08:10.975 --> 00:08:13.600
you, I don't know.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.110
But I love you is empty.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.833
It is mainstream.

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.380
- [Thoraya] So it's not
that you don't want to

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.590
find this connection, you
just don't want to express it

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.800
in those ways.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:26.783
- I don't know, I mean does
connection really exist?

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.550
- [Thoraya] Do you believe in love?

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.310
- Oh yeah, of course.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.550
- [Thoraya] So your sister went before you

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.576
and she doesn't.

00:08:33.576 --> 00:08:35.050
- Yeah, she doesn't.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:35.990
She doesn't.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.770
But yes, I believe in love.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.880
I hope to find someone
really special to me,

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.880
and I don't know, maybe
spend all my life with him.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.830
- It was Halloween.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:56.200
I was Tigerlily and he was Captain Hook.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.020
We had a Halloween party at my house.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.410
We were in my room.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:03.801
I think maybe I was like
holding his face in my hands.

00:09:03.801 --> 00:09:05.523
(laughing)

00:09:05.523 --> 00:09:08.920
And I said, don't make me say it.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.063
Don't make me say that I love you.

00:09:11.996 --> 00:09:12.946
It was really nice.

00:09:20.776 --> 00:09:25.776
- So, I guess the last
time I felt like the words

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:29.130
I love you I really needed to say

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.930
was when I left my home in San Jose

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:34.070
to come here to San Diego.

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:36.460
I really felt like I needed
to say it to my parents.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.220
I really didn't tell
them my plan or intention

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.320
of moving down here in San
Diego, and me and my parents,

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.970
we don't really have a great relationship

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.650
in terms of being
communicative and expressing

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.300
our feelings towards each other.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.430
You know, I've been in San
Diego for almost four years,

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:53.580
and I've only seen my parents
once or twice every year.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:56.070
The further I am away from them,

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.810
I really feel like, man,
I really wish I said

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.052
I love you to them when I left.

00:10:01.052 --> 00:10:03.820
And to this day, too,
it's a struggle for me

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.160
to say I love you to my parents.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.260
And if I could say it
right now, I would say it,

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.160
like a million times.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.493
You know what I mean?

00:10:12.521 --> 00:10:14.997
- [Thoraya] Would you be
down to call them right now?

00:10:14.997 --> 00:10:15.830
- Sure.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.391
- [Thoraya] And tell them you love them?

00:10:17.391 --> 00:10:18.224
- You know what, yeah.

00:10:18.224 --> 00:10:19.210
I'm gonna call my mom right now.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.960
I want to tell her that I love her.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.200
- [Thoraya] Okay, there you go.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.033
- I'm gonna do it right now.

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:24.080
Wow.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:24.913
Hello, mom?

00:10:31.086 --> 00:10:32.336
I love you mom.

00:10:35.986 --> 00:10:37.486
I'm sorry, I know.

00:11:09.863 --> 00:11:10.926
Yeah, yeah. I know.

00:11:10.926 --> 00:11:11.759
I'm sorry.

00:11:20.735 --> 00:11:22.111
Oh.

00:11:22.111 --> 00:11:22.944
Yeah.

00:11:27.306 --> 00:11:28.139
Yeah.

00:11:35.043 --> 00:11:35.876
Wow, okay.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.163
Oh wow, really?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:49.763
Oh.

00:11:49.763 --> 00:11:50.596
All right, well.

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:54.999
Bye, mom.

00:11:54.999 --> 00:11:56.290
It was like a little bit of lecture,

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.190
a little bit of tough
love, a little bit of

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.070
what are you doing with
your life, a little bit

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.650
of all that, but at the
end of it, you know.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.930
She was just like making
sure that I was okay.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:07.160
I sometimes get into a
deep space where I feel

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.343
like nobody's watching me.

00:12:08.343 --> 00:12:11.360
Just because, you know,
being in this big city

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.193
you're really,

00:12:14.196 --> 00:12:15.273
it really took a toll on me just thinking

00:12:15.273 --> 00:12:16.510
that I was alone.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:20.410
But I always remember that I
made a lot of friends here,

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:23.158
and I have a business
partner, and I have my family.

00:12:23.158 --> 00:12:26.840
I have the grace of God
just watching over me,

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.530
so I'm not completely alone.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:31.643
It's just at times that are tough,

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:33.970
I love you is really powerful,

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:35.603
so I'm so glad I said it.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.190
- So, for me the most
memorable moment I have

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.470
where I said I love you was to my late mom

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:45.550
who passed away, I'd say
around three years ago.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:47.810
It was on her death bed
where I did say I love you.

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:49.680
I do remember around like two months prior

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.140
is when she started to lose her voice.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.060
It was getting very straining
for her to do anything at all.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:56.140
She was mostly bedridden
for that last two months

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.060
that we had her here.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.470
It was one dark night.

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:01.570
Me, my dad, and her were
all together in the room.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.750
And we were just, as you
know, we normally did

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.000
during that time, we were
just together in silence,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.010
not really saying anything.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.290
There wasn't really much
that needed to be said.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:12.479
At one point, my dad did
kind of close in on me.

00:13:12.479 --> 00:13:15.630
He like stood next to my
ear and he whispered to me

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:18.290
that it's okay to cry,
and you know when you hear

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.600
those words in those types of situations

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:22.020
you tend to let go.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.630
So obviously I ended up crying, sobbing,

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.530
all that ugly stuff that no
one really wants to go through.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.950
And I hope no one does, ever.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:29.783
But,

00:13:32.505 --> 00:13:34.630
and I do remember with
my head down sobbing

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.670
she put her hands up to my
hair and started playing

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:41.080
with my hair, like how she
did when I was a little kid.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.100
And so I look up, she's staring at me,

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:44.930
and I tell her, I love you mom.

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:45.890
I love you.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:47.860
And she said it back, to which obviously,

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.970
I wouldn't say I lost it,
for lack of a better word.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.420
But it really did hit really deep for me.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:58.170
I don't think I've ever
received or have experienced

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.477
any type of that love, like
when she said I love you,

00:14:00.477 --> 00:14:03.703
it not only was like loud and clear,

00:14:03.703 --> 00:14:05.763
it had this weight to it, you know.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.500
When she said I love you,
I really did feel that

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.250
all throughout my body and
all throughout my head, too.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.770
And so I'm really glad that I was able

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.400
to experience that one last time at least

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.550
before she passed away.

00:14:18.896 --> 00:14:21.979
(gentle piano music)

00:14:25.582 --> 00:14:28.300
- Hey everyone, happy
early Valentine's Day.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.900
As always, thank you for
watching another episode.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:33.450
If you enjoy watching
my videos, and you want

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.630
to watch more, please make sure
to hit the subscribe button

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:39.140
and the bell next to it
os you'll get notified

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.380
every Thursday morning when I upload.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.660
Thank you guys again for everything,

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:45.353
and I'll see you next week.

